1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,650
Episode five used two link targets,
and episode eight added a third.

2
00:00:04,722 --> 00:00:08,482
Five are left, and Go to Sibling
has an edge case worth knowing.

3
00:00:08,626 --> 00:00:11,456
Most of them sit on this
day page's top bar.

4
00:00:12,653 --> 00:00:15,873
Click 2026: Go to Specific Page.

5
00:00:15,971 --> 00:00:20,671
It names one page, 2026 Planner,
instead of a relationship.

6
00:00:20,710 --> 00:00:24,600
Home would be three levels up from
a day, but four from a journal.

7
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:27,300
A fixed page is right on every template.

8
00:00:27,506 --> 00:00:29,946
It's also how you jump across the tree.

9
00:00:29,979 --> 00:00:35,059
On Week View, a Notes chip: T for text,
and a box at the end of the top bar.

10
00:00:35,921 --> 00:00:40,901
Go to Specific Page, then Select Target
Page, and pick Notes from the tree.

11
00:00:40,990 --> 00:00:44,090
Now all fifty-three weeks
open the same Notes list.

12
00:00:45,324 --> 00:00:49,330
On Day View, the Journal chip
is Go to Child (by Index).

13
00:00:49,421 --> 00:00:54,721
Target Child lists this day's pages, but
it stores a position: zero, the first.

14
00:00:54,925 --> 00:00:57,975
So every day's chip opens
that day's own Journal.

15
00:00:58,106 --> 00:01:02,976
Use it when every page of a kind has
the same sub-pages, in the same order.

16
00:01:03,191 --> 00:01:05,901
The right arrow is Go
to Sibling, plus one.

17
00:01:05,947 --> 00:01:09,707
But January 31 is the last day in January.

18
00:01:09,759 --> 00:01:14,410
The link doesn't wrap around; it climbs
to Quarter 1 and takes the next month's

19
00:01:14,410 --> 00:01:15,249
first day.

20
00:01:15,454 --> 00:01:16,854
One level only.

21
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:21,322
March 31's next day sits under
Quarter 2, two levels away,

22
00:01:21,322 --> 00:01:23,990
so March 31 gets no right arrow.

23
00:01:24,118 --> 00:01:26,998
The editor still draws it; the PDF won't.

24
00:01:27,072 --> 00:01:31,872
Any next sibling will do, though: Quarter
4's right arrow opens the Weeks list.

25
00:01:32,119 --> 00:01:36,740
Q1 is Go to Ancestor (Level), two
levels up: from a day to its month,

26
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:38,129
then its quarter.

27
00:01:38,184 --> 00:01:41,414
Use it when the page you want
is further up than the parent.

28
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:44,480
The count starts from the
page that draws the chip.

29
00:01:44,562 --> 00:01:48,962
Journals sit a level lower, so the
Journal template's Q1 says three.

30
00:01:49,088 --> 00:01:52,988
Ask for more levels than a page
has, and the chip is left off.

31
00:01:53,194 --> 00:01:55,940
Month View's week labels
need something else.

32
00:01:55,976 --> 00:01:59,724
No week references a month;
weeks reference its days.

33
00:01:59,817 --> 00:02:03,337
So Go to Child's Referrer asks
about the month's children.

34
00:02:03,542 --> 00:02:09,862
Start Index is the last day in the
label's row: 6-month_start_offset.

35
00:02:09,954 --> 00:02:13,544
Count / Direction, minus seven,
walks back up to a week.

36
00:02:13,648 --> 00:02:16,168
The first day a week references wins.

37
00:02:16,374 --> 00:02:20,924
The filter prefers references on one
template, and falls back to any.

38
00:02:20,982 --> 00:02:25,065
One trap: the count is ignored
until Start Index holds a value,

39
00:02:25,065 --> 00:02:28,102
though that box shows
zero when it's empty.

40
00:02:28,307 --> 00:02:32,197
Open URL is the one target
that leaves the PDF.

41
00:02:32,327 --> 00:02:36,548
On the Year View template, the cover
gets a web address near the bottom,

42
00:02:36,548 --> 00:02:38,967
black on black until I make it white.

43
00:02:39,186 --> 00:02:44,323
On Click, Open URL, and the whole
address, starting with https.

44
00:02:44,418 --> 00:02:49,038
It's stored exactly as typed, and most
readers can't open a bare address.

45
00:02:49,277 --> 00:02:53,497
There's nothing in the tree to resolve,
so the exporter never hides it.

46
00:02:53,547 --> 00:02:57,477
With the box empty, the line
would still print, as plain text.

47
00:02:57,682 --> 00:03:00,877
Deleting is where links
and references part ways.

48
00:03:01,026 --> 00:03:04,555
In Hierarchy, I'll select
Week 2: our Notes chip,

49
00:03:04,555 --> 00:03:07,326
and January 5 and 6 in its top row.

50
00:03:07,699 --> 00:03:10,369
First, the reference to January 5.

51
00:03:10,498 --> 00:03:15,014
The dialog says only the reference
goes, and the page stays where it is.

52
00:03:15,085 --> 00:03:18,795
The week loses its Monday,
and January keeps its fifth.

53
00:03:19,625 --> 00:03:21,575
Now the real January 6.

54
00:03:21,718 --> 00:03:26,428
Its Journal and Daily Notes go with it,
and so does its reference in Week 2.

55
00:03:26,508 --> 00:03:29,116
Nothing is left pointing
at a missing page.

56
00:03:29,810 --> 00:03:32,340
And a fixed link can't outlive its page.

57
00:03:32,412 --> 00:03:35,832
Delete Notes, and the chip's
On Click drops back to None.

58
00:03:35,978 --> 00:03:38,408
The chip still prints, as plain text.

59
00:03:38,613 --> 00:03:42,843
Control Z, three times, and all
three come back, link included.

60
00:03:43,048 --> 00:03:44,718
Let's export and check.

61
00:03:44,812 --> 00:03:47,092
Thirteen hundred pages take a moment.

62
00:03:47,198 --> 00:03:52,777
Links are only worked out here, page by
page, so the PDF is the only place to test

63
00:03:52,777 --> 00:03:53,368
them.

64
00:03:53,572 --> 00:03:57,457
The cover's address line is a live
link, but it would leave the reader,

65
00:03:57,457 --> 00:03:58,802
so I won't click it.

66
00:03:59,006 --> 00:04:02,936
Quarter 1, then January 31
in its little calendar.

67
00:04:03,030 --> 00:04:07,180
The right arrow lands on February
1, the next month's first day.

68
00:04:07,388 --> 00:04:10,565
Journal opens this day's
own journal, and its Q1,

69
00:04:10,565 --> 00:04:13,538
three levels up, goes back to the quarter.

70
00:04:13,745 --> 00:04:15,355
Now March 31.

71
00:04:15,420 --> 00:04:20,030
There's a left arrow, but no right one:
the next day lives in another quarter.

72
00:04:20,235 --> 00:04:21,855
Mar goes up to March.

73
00:04:21,888 --> 00:04:26,778
Its sixth week label scans back
to March 31 and finds Week 14.

74
00:04:26,906 --> 00:04:29,986
And Week 14's Notes chip
opens the Notes list.

75
00:04:30,549 --> 00:04:34,479
That's every kind of link, and what
each does when there's nowhere to go.

76
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:37,410
Next time: getting your
planner onto a tablet.
